Where are they?

754
00:56:55,120 --> 00:56:56,246
They're safe.

755
00:56:56,997 --> 00:56:57,998
Here,

756
00:56:58,081 --> 00:56:59,166
in Paris.

757
00:56:59,207 --> 00:57:01,168
They'll be safer
in my hands.

758
00:57:19,311 --> 00:57:20,729
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

759
00:57:23,565 --> 00:57:25,067
(CELL PHONE BEEPS)

760
00:57:30,072 --> 00:57:32,991
You know, as a cop you see
some pretty weird shit.

761
00:57:33,033 --> 00:57:35,243
But I have to be
honest with you.

762
00:57:35,327 --> 00:57:37,579
What you did back there,
that freaked me out.

763
00:57:38,121 --> 00:57:39,957
To put everyone
to sleep like that.

764
00:57:40,540 --> 00:57:42,459
Do I need to be worried?

765
00:57:42,751 --> 00:57:43,877
No.

766
00:57:45,212 --> 00:57:46,463
Good.

767
00:57:50,342 --> 00:57:52,344
(INDISTINCT VOICES CHATTERING)

768
00:58:01,019 --> 00:58:02,646
(MAN'S VOICE GROWS LOUDER)

769
00:58:08,068 --> 00:58:09,444
Do you mind?

770
00:58:09,861 --> 00:58:10,862
No.

771
00:58:13,740 --> 00:58:16,243
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

772
00:58:28,755 --> 00:58:31,883
What's that?
Korean. I'm gonna drive.

773
00:58:32,551 --> 00:58:34,886
Hey! No, no, no.
This is a police car!

774
00:58:35,512 --> 00:58:38,306
You can't. No, this is
not possible, lady.

775
00:58:38,473 --> 00:58:39,641
This is a police car.

776
00:58:42,185 --> 00:58:43,437
Okay, okay.

777
00:58:51,528 --> 00:58:52,529
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

778
00:58:57,159 --> 00:58:59,161
Sir, sir, excuse me, sir.

779
00:58:59,494 --> 00:59:00,787
I need to talk
to somebody.

780
00:59:01,121 --> 00:59:02,456
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

781
00:59:03,040 --> 00:59:05,625
Look, I'm a German
citizen and I demand
to see a lawyer.

782
00:59:05,959 --> 00:59:07,252
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

783
00:59:36,573 --> 00:59:37,908
(TIRES SCREECHING)

784
00:59:38,325 --> 00:59:39,409
Do you always
drive like that?

785
00:59:39,493 --> 00:59:40,827
I've never driven before.

786
00:59:41,369 --> 00:59:42,370
Great.

787
00:59:48,293 --> 00:59:50,295
Hey, that's one-way.
We're late.

788
01:00:12,734 --> 01:00:14,152
Hey, I'd rather be
late than dead.

789
01:00:14,277 --> 01:00:15,529
We never really die.

790
01:01:05,370 --> 01:01:06,746
Sorry, sir.

791
01:01:07,080 --> 01:01:08,165
I don't feel good.

792
01:01:08,623 --> 01:01:09,624
(MAN GRUNTS)

793
01:01:11,251 --> 01:01:12,252
(PANTING)

794
01:01:15,338 --> 01:01:17,841
I'm fine. I'm fine.

795
01:01:22,470 --> 01:01:23,680
(CARS HONKING)

796
01:01:26,266 --> 01:01:27,642
(SIRENS WAILING)

797
01:01:30,270 --> 01:01:31,605
I'm gonna tell them
to stop following us.

798
01:01:31,771 --> 01:01:32,772
Don't bother.

799
01:01:37,819 --> 01:01:39,613
(BEEPING)

800
01:02:15,815 --> 01:02:16,816
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

801
01:02:34,834 --> 01:02:36,211
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

802
01:02:55,438 --> 01:02:56,439
Give me the case.

803
01:02:56,898 --> 01:02:57,899
(LAUGHS)

804
01:02:58,400 --> 01:02:59,859
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

805
01:03:06,866 --> 01:03:07,867
(GRUNTS)

806
01:03:12,247 --> 01:03:13,248
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

807
01:03:44,279 --> 01:03:45,280
Ahhh!

808
01:03:54,205 --> 01:03:55,206
(GROANING)

809
01:04:07,427 --> 01:04:08,428
Open it.

810
01:04:13,266 --> 01:04:14,601
(SQUELCHING)

811
01:04:22,233 --> 01:04:23,276
Let's go.

812
01:04:23,526 --> 01:04:25,445
I'm not sure I could
be of any help for you.

813
01:04:30,700 --> 01:04:31,701
Yes, you are.

814
01:04:32,619 --> 01:04:33,620
What for?

815
01:04:40,418 --> 01:04:41,795
A reminder.

816
01:04:42,921 --> 01:04:44,255
Shall we go?

817
01:05:03,733 --> 01:05:05,402
(PEOPLE CLAMORING)

818
01:05:12,117 --> 01:05:13,118
Where are we going?

819
01:05:13,660 --> 01:05:15,203
ELECTRONIC VOICE:
<i>Take the first left.</i>

820
01:05:17,497 --> 01:05:18,581
Okay.

821
01:05:29,676 --> 01:05:30,677
(OFFICER SPEAKING FRENCH)

822
01:05:34,556 --> 01:05:36,015
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

823
01:05:39,811 --> 01:05:40,895
(CELL PHONE RINGING)
Professor?

824
01:05:41,980 --> 01:05:43,398
Hello?
<i>Lucy.</i>

825
01:05:43,523 --> 01:05:45,442
Oh! It's her! It's her!

826
01:05:45,650 --> 01:05:47,444
Hey, you.

827
01:05:47,527 --> 01:05:49,279
You're in Paris?
<i>Yes, I am.</i>

828
01:05:49,362 --> 01:05:51,030
Good, good! Excellent.

829
01:05:51,239 --> 01:05:54,534
So, look,
I am no longer
at the hotel now.

830
01:05:54,617 --> 01:05:56,244
I have come
to the university,

831
01:05:56,327 --> 01:05:57,704
where I've taken
the liberty

832
01:05:57,745 --> 01:06:00,832
of calling together
a few of my colleagues
to discuss your case.

833
01:06:00,874 --> 01:06:04,043
Top minds in their field
and very trustworthy.

834
01:06:04,085 --> 01:06:05,378
<i>I trust you.</i>

835
01:06:05,545 --> 01:06:06,546
Oh, thank you.

836
01:06:06,713 --> 01:06:07,881
So, do you think
you could meet us

837
01:06:07,922 --> 01:06:10,049
here at the university?
(LINE DISCONNECTS)

838
01:06:13,720 --> 01:06:14,929
I'm, uh...

839
01:06:15,680 --> 01:06:17,015
I'm very pleased
to meet you.

840
01:06:17,140 --> 01:06:18,224
Likewise.

841
01:06:18,725 --> 01:06:19,809
Captain Del Rio.

842
01:06:19,976 --> 01:06:21,311
How do you do?

843
01:06:21,561 --> 01:06:22,562
Um...

844
01:06:22,854 --> 01:06:25,773
Let me introduce
you to my colleagues.

845
01:06:25,940 --> 01:06:28,318
This is Professor Cartier,
neurosurgeon.

846
01:06:28,651 --> 01:06:30,570
I know who everyone is.

847
01:06:31,863 --> 01:06:33,156
Of course.

848
01:06:33,573 --> 01:06:37,243
Gentlemen, this is Lucy,
the first woman to...

849
01:06:37,994 --> 01:06:39,579
I mean...

850
01:06:39,621 --> 01:06:42,957
As I mentioned earlier,
Miss Lucy has,

851
01:06:43,041 --> 01:06:45,210
for reasons that
remain a mystery to me,

852
01:06:45,251 --> 01:06:48,963
unlocked certain
portions of her brain

853
01:06:49,047 --> 01:06:51,841
that offer access to

854
01:06:51,925 --> 01:06:54,511
previously unexplored
cerebral zones.

855
01:06:55,386 --> 01:06:57,597
She has abilities.

856
01:06:58,306 --> 01:06:59,599
Can you give us
an example?

857
01:07:00,141 --> 01:07:01,726
Your daughter,
Gabrielle, age six,

858
01:07:01,768 --> 01:07:02,977
died in a car accident.

859
01:07:03,686 --> 01:07:05,271
It was a blue car,
leather seats,

860
01:07:05,855 --> 01:07:08,024
<i>plastic bird hanging
from the rear view mirror.</i>
(GIRL LAUGHING)

861
01:07:08,691 --> 01:07:09,692
(SOBBING)

862
01:07:24,499 --> 01:07:26,251
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

863
01:07:49,649 --> 01:07:51,192
There are men coming here.
Can you secure the room?

864
01:07:51,609 --> 01:07:52,652
I need to stay focused.

865
01:07:52,694 --> 01:07:53,695
Sure.

866
01:07:57,448 --> 01:07:58,825
(SIRENS WAILING)

867
01:07:59,534 --> 01:08:00,618
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

868
01:08:03,413 --> 01:08:04,664
(OFFICERS SHOUTING)

869
01:08:10,837 --> 01:08:13,172
How did you manage to access
all this information?

870
01:08:13,214 --> 01:08:14,924
Electrical impulses.

871
01:08:15,008 --> 01:08:17,969
Every cell knows and talks
to every other cell.

872
01:08:18,011 --> 01:08:21,347
They exchange a thousand
bits of information
between them per second.

873
01:08:21,472 --> 01:08:25,018
Cells group together,
forming a giant
web of communication,

874
01:08:25,101 --> 01:08:26,436
which in turn forms matter.

875
01:08:27,729 --> 01:08:30,481
Cells get together,
take on one form,

876
01:08:31,357 --> 01:08:33,026
deform, reform.

877
01:08:33,234 --> 01:08:35,653
Makes no difference,
it's all the same.

878
01:08:36,321 --> 01:08:38,239
<i>Humans consider
themselves unique,</i>

879
01:08:38,323 --> 01:08:39,866
<i>so they've rooted
their whole theory</i>

880
01:08:39,949 --> 01:08:41,784
<i>of existence on
their uniqueness.</i>

881
01:08:42,035 --> 01:08:43,786
"One" is their
unit of measure.

882
01:08:43,870 --> 01:08:45,163
But it's not.

883
01:08:45,204 --> 01:08:48,374
All social systems
we've put into place
are a mere sketch.

884
01:08:48,458 --> 01:08:51,044
One plus one equals two.
That's all we've learned.

885
01:08:51,085 --> 01:08:54,213
But one plus one
has never equaled two.

886
01:08:54,255 --> 01:08:57,216
There are, in fact,
no numbers and no letters.

887
01:08:57,342 --> 01:09:00,887
We've codified
our existence to bring
it down to human size

888
01:09:00,970 --> 01:09:02,972
to make it comprehensible.

889
01:09:03,056 --> 01:09:07,644
We've created a scale
so that we can forget
its unfathomable scale.

890
01:09:11,230 --> 01:09:13,399
But if humans are
not the unit of measure

891
01:09:13,816 --> 01:09:16,569
<i>and the world
isn't governed by
mathematical laws,</i>

892
01:09:17,820 --> 01:09:19,072
what governs all that?

893
01:09:21,199 --> 01:09:23,076
Film a car
speeding down a road.

894
01:09:23,409 --> 01:09:25,703
Speed up the image
infinitely

895
01:09:26,537 --> 01:09:28,414
and the car disappears.

896
01:09:31,417 --> 01:09:34,253
So what proof do we
have of its existence?

897
01:09:34,629 --> 01:09:37,215
Time gives legitimacy
to its existence.

898
01:09:37,256 --> 01:09:40,093
Time is the only
true unit of measure.

899
01:09:40,551 --> 01:09:43,388
<i>It gives proof to
the existence of matter.</i>

900
01:09:43,930 --> 01:09:45,348
Without time,

901
01:09:46,182 --> 01:09:47,725
we don't exist.

902
01:09:54,440 --> 01:09:55,525
Time is unity.

903
01:09:55,692 --> 01:09:57,276
(ALARMS BLARING)

904
01:10:03,950 --> 01:10:05,785
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

905
01:10:10,123 --> 01:10:11,958
We won't be able to
hold them for much longer.

906
01:10:13,334 --> 01:10:14,961
Time to go then.

907
01:10:28,099 --> 01:10:30,560
Are you sure you
need such huge doses?

908
01:10:30,977 --> 01:10:32,478
I'm afraid
you won't survive.

909
01:10:32,562 --> 01:10:34,439
Some cells
inside me will fight

910
01:10:34,480 --> 01:10:36,065
and defend their
integrity till
the very end.

911
01:10:36,733 --> 01:10:40,361
In order to attain
the last few percent,
I have to force it

912
01:10:40,528 --> 01:10:42,822
to crack the cells open
to their nucleus.

913
01:10:43,698 --> 01:10:44,699
(SIGHS)

914
01:10:51,998 --> 01:10:54,250
But all of this
knowledge, Lucy...

915
01:10:56,169 --> 01:10:58,796
I'm not even sure that
mankind is ready for it.

916
01:10:59,046 --> 01:11:01,758
We're so driven by
power and profit.

917
01:11:02,175 --> 01:11:03,926
Given man's nature,

918
01:11:05,136 --> 01:11:08,347
it might bring us only
instability and chaos.

919
01:11:12,560 --> 01:11:15,021
Ignorance brings chaos,
not knowledge.

920
01:11:15,313 --> 01:11:18,316
I'll build a computer
and download all
my knowledge in it.

921
01:11:18,524 --> 01:11:21,444
I'll find a way for you
to have access to it.

922
01:11:21,903 --> 01:11:23,029
Yeah.

923
01:11:23,780 --> 01:11:27,033
I just hope we will be
worthy of your sacrifice.

924
01:11:37,293 --> 01:11:38,544
Nobody move!

925
01:11:48,471 --> 01:11:49,847
(BREATHING DEEPLY)

926
01:11:55,853 --> 01:11:57,980
Do you understand English?

927
01:12:21,170 --> 01:12:22,171
(GUNFIRE)

928
01:12:22,839 --> 01:12:23,840
(GASPING)

929
01:13:00,126 --> 01:13:01,460
PROFESSOR: What is she doing?

930
01:13:01,544 --> 01:13:03,880
NORMAN: She's looking
for energy and matter.

931
01:13:08,217 --> 01:13:11,512
And she's trying to connect
with our computers.

932
01:13:51,761 --> 01:13:53,638
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

933
01:14:05,191 --> 01:14:06,192
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

934
01:14:14,825 --> 01:14:16,243
PROFESSOR 1: Oh, my God.
What's happening?

935
01:14:27,254 --> 01:14:28,381
PROFESSOR 2:
What is she making?

936
01:14:29,173 --> 01:14:31,801
New generation computer,
I presume.

937
01:15:11,549 --> 01:15:12,550
(SHOUTING IN FRENCH)

938
01:15:20,224 --> 01:15:21,600
(INDISTINCT VOICES CHATTERING)

939
01:16:39,678 --> 01:16:41,138
(TROLLEY BELL RINGING)

940
01:16:44,809 --> 01:16:46,018
(HORSE NEIGHING)

941
01:17:19,718 --> 01:17:21,011
(DISTANT SCREECHING)

942
01:17:25,558 --> 01:17:26,559
(GRUNTING)

943
01:17:32,565 --> 01:17:33,566
(ROARING)

944
01:17:36,318 --> 01:17:37,862
(HUFFING)

945
01:17:47,246 --> 01:17:48,247
(SNARLS)

946
01:17:48,372 --> 01:17:49,373
(HUFFING)

947
01:20:51,263 --> 01:20:52,264
(SPEAKING KOREAN)

948
01:21:01,857 --> 01:21:03,150
Hey, you!

949
01:21:15,788 --> 01:21:17,539
(BREATHING DEEPLY)

950
01:21:20,042 --> 01:21:22,419
PROFESSOR: Look.
The computer, it's moving.

951
01:21:48,862 --> 01:21:49,947
DEL RIO: Hey.

952
01:21:50,989 --> 01:21:52,074
Where is she?

953
01:21:54,868 --> 01:21:56,120
(CELL PHONE BEEPS)

954
01:22:21,270 --> 01:22:24,690
LUCY: <i>Life was given to
us a billion years ago.</i>

955
01:22:24,940 --> 01:22:27,276
<i>Now you know
what to do with it.</i>

